tps://api.github.com/users/momosnn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/momosnn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/momosnn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/momosnn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/momosnn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/momosnn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/momosnn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-07-09T14:04:01Z","updated_at":"2019-07-09T14:08:04Z","body":"Hey Chris, I've still only managed to load in 1.5TB of data so far. \r\n\r\nI can confirm that the leveldb2 metadatastore consumes a LOT less CPU. The issue was still present in v1.39 (but with 40% CPU instead of 130%). I was also seeing long delays of about 12 seconds for each request during one of my runs (when I performed a lot of overwrites on the same set of files). So looks like there was some kind of contention issue.\r\n\r\nv1.40 seems to have fixed the high CPU problem so I think you can close this issue. You fixed another bug with the file listings and hashes also. Thanks for all your effort.\r\n\r\nI've had some problems trying to get my clients to push through with maximum throughput. I'm assuming it's not SeaweedFS's fault but probably my disks or the database. I'll report back if I find anything.\r\n\r\nThanks again.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/comments/509656018/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/comments/509656778","html_url":"https://github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/996#issuecomment-509656778","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/issues/996","id":509656778